      "title": "One mic, two mixes",
      "summary": "Play the vocal signal, then move either fader. The two meters follow the same voice at independently set levels.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "illustration",
          "view": "landscape",
          "passage": "At a small gig, the singer’s microphone feeds two mixes. One goes to the audience through the main speakers. The other goes to the singer through a floor monitor. During soundcheck, the audience hears a clear vocal, but the singer can barely hear herself. The engineer raises only the monitor send. Now the singer hears more voice while the audience mix stays the same. During the chorus, the engineer raises only the main vocal fader. This time the audience hears the lift and the singer’s monitor stays where it was. The monitor send is taken before the main fader, which is what makes those two changes independent.",
